            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Huh. Maybe there's something going on on my side then, I'll look into that.\r\n\r\nWould you mind adding a follow up here if/when you figure it out?\r\n\r\n> However, it's not an actual `filetype` as far as neovim is concerned (it's still only recognized as `elixir`, which makes sense since it's the same thing within). But there _is_ a dedicated icon for those so maybe we still want to make use of it? I guess it would be similar to `.h` files that are still `C` code, but come with their own mappings.\r\n\r\nIf it is not an actual filetype (i.e. a value of 'filetype' option when you open such files), then it will not have an entry in \"filetype\" category.\r\n\r\nI am open to changing \"exs\" extension have \"\" icon (i.e. \"nf-seti-elixir_script\" class), but I would like to ask to for some reputable sources that this is the icon that to be used for \"exs\" extensions.",
